# Keep text stable so diffs show CONTENT, not line endings.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS EXISTS: this machine has core.autocrlf = true at the SYSTEM level,
# with nothing overriding it. Without a committed .gitattributes, git decides
# line endings by itself and two things follow:
#
#   - A CRLF-only difference presents as a WHOLE-FILE change. During the doc
#     consolidation, rest_api.md showed a 139-line diff between two copies that
#     were byte-identical once line endings were stripped. That noise makes
#     "is this version newer?" much harder to answer.
#   - core.autocrlf is a MACHINE setting, not a committed one. The machine that
#     builds the TV side may have it set differently, so the same file can
#     round-trip differently on the two machines.
#
# ⭐ A committed .gitattributes travels with the clone and removes both.
# ⓘ aurora-tv and ds5-webos-bridge already have one; ctm-bridge-webos is next.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.inl  text eol=lf
*.cpp  text eol=lf
*.cs   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.map     text eol=lf
*.profile text eol=lf

# Windows tooling expects CRLF here.
# ⓘ .ps1 is deliberately CRLF: PowerShell tolerates LF, but a BOM-less LF
# here-string can behave differently, and every .ps1 in the working tree is
# already CRLF.
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.sln     text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj text eol=crlf
*.filters text eol=crlf
*.xaml    text eol=crlf
*.rc      text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.exe binary
*.wav binary
